["<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Tinker et al. v. Des Moines Independent Community School District et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/3d478d7f-683e-425e-b056-164ea26c17b5.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1518/1547\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\n[underlined: Reverse]\nCan reverse on very narrow ground -\nequal protection - too strictly and\nsingled out a particular kind of\nconduct -\n— Do not take away legitimate sta of\nschool boards -\n— Equal protection -\n— No bad conduct involved here -</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Street v. New York</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/4e378af1-69ce-47af-83f9-001a13af8ba2.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1533/1263\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\n[underlined: Affirm] on opinion of Court of Appeals of N.Y. —\nFuld&#x27;s opinion limited to the one point\nof the burning of the flag —\nConduct and not speech or symbolic\nspeech —\nComplaint of police officer reciting\nspeech does not change the point —</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Street v. New York</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/31a85c7c-ba6c-4a8e-a498-8d057420481d.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1621/730\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Black, J.\n[underlined: Affirm] would be bothered if he\nthought NY meant to punish speech\nWould divide the statute</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Street v. New York</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/37cc8d00-3f70-4639-8a4e-3e21ce51bb83.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:528/349\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Douglas, J.\n[underlined: Pass]</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Street v. New York</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/0ed75c2a-bf4a-4d54-bf8e-957dbb2d1736.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1740/2027\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Harlan, J.\n[underlined: Reverse]\nWould not deal with statute on its face\nJudg is ambiguous —\n—\nWe should look at record — charge put\nthe speech element in issue —\n—\nAbsent any indication of what judge\nrelied on — would reverse\n—\nCould have been on verbal point\n—\nStay away from statute —\n\n[underlined: Reverse] and [underlined: remand]</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Street v. New York</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/46c88871-26cd-4ee6-a964-2e408d6777ed.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1743/1595\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Brennan, J.\n[underlined: Reverse]\nAgree with JMH on the record -- can not\ndetermine which way court went -\nRead all the opinion could say and\nlimit - Πs waived the other point so\nwhat could be said\n[underlined: NB] Re-read O&#x27;Brien carefully -\nthis a burning in protest -\nState interest in going against flag burning -</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Epperson et al. v. Arkansas</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/15951ac1-7485-4058-ad17-ce7fb0bb35de.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1233/925\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>C. J.\nHave to reverse but how -\n[underlined: Statute] [underlined: vague] and therefore vague -\n[underlined: No] state need shown -\nuse Butler v Michigan case -</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Epperson et al. v. Arkansas</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/c794638c-8313-444f-858f-5d2960701807.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1066/1130\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Black J.\nnot convinced on all issues\nWill go with too vague&quot;\nbut no further -\nnever been an effort to enforce\nthe law - no case or controversy</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Epperson et al. v. Arkansas</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/ac6e8dbd-a7c2-45dc-bc9d-251ba2df6d9e.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1143/999\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Douglas, J.\nVagueness enough for\n[underlined: him]\nEstablishmt of religion\nis not in the case\nDo [underlined: not] use Butler v\n[underlined: Michigan]</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Epperson et al. v. Arkansas</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/00f2df19-a60b-4f21-a50e-61920e3e4272.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1185/772\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Harlan, J.\nEstablishment is here - must be\nsome way to get it back to\nArkansas court.\n—\nHe would affirm</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Epperson et al. v. Arkansas</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/fda0b302-c7b2-424a-8183-ea73a1140c86.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:954/512\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Brennan, J.\nLimit to Vagueness\nuse [underlined: Butler]</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Epperson et al. v. Arkansas</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/19293584-a693-488d-9626-a6b52cfb6520.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1255/1156\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Stewart, J.\nDonot see Butler\n\nTrouble with vagueness\npoint\nSC of Arkansas makes it\nvague,\n\n1^st Amendment rt. of\nteacher to say what he wants\n\nDonot get to curriculum point</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Epperson et al. v. Arkansas</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/5a50c1f0-3894-4662-ac1f-d8a5b3d2488e.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1153/448\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>White, J.\nMight go on vagueness - but\nCan&#x27;t see where it is vague -</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Epperson et al. v. Arkansas</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/44d38bca-7e76-4139-8d03-acae286ff8f4.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1060/1107\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Fortas, J.\nNarrow ground - establishment\nis the ground to be used -\n—\nLaw &quot;blocks out&quot; theory of\nevolution -\n—\nEstablishment only -\nW vagueness</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Epperson et al. v. Arkansas</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/fd8cd4a5-8367-4c19-aeb5-5cf1e43a6d79.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1073/564\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Marshall, J.\nEstablishment only —\nFollow [underlined: AF]</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by Lewis F. Powell Jr</p><h2>Leary v. United States</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/9b1b1c9b-5dc0-40c4-9369-2bbeb1a5d0aa.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2117\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\nCan&#x27;t agree with app&#x27;tmg &quot;tie breaker&quot;.\n[struck: ID] No [inserted: need to] write an opinion.\nDeny N.M. motion to dismiss\nHave Master reconsider the &quot;double\nmass analysis&quot;.\n\nJustice Brennan\n[struck: ID] &quot;No&quot; as to tie-breaker.\nSpecial Master should redefine the\n&#x27;47 Condition + go ahead + decide issues\nNeed a new S/M.\n\nJustice White\nBreitstein is outraged by failure of\nlawyers to get together. [struck: Fa] He is very able.\n[struck: Practice must]\nOn merits, we can&#x27;t appt a tie breaker.\nNor do [underlined: we] have auth. to decide\nissues left to Comm.\nSustain whatever Exceptions are\n[struck: nec] necessary to return case to S/M.\nMust rely on Experts — this is\nan arbitrary choice</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by Lewis F. Powell Jr</p><h2>Leary v. United States</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/2b36fa6c-6da3-4c46-80ed-0cf8ff5504b9.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2117\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Justice Marshall\nAgree with BRW\n\nJustice Blackmun\nAgree generally with #BRW\n\nJustice Powell\nSee my notes on p 2 of Report.</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1968 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by Lewis F. Powell Jr</p><h2>Leary v. United States</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/41d96cd2-ff3a-4c47-84aa-9981df08855c.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2117\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Justice Rehnquist\n[struck: Stot]\nNo Tiebreaker\nAgree with S/M as to double mass\n\nJustice Stevens\nS/M Report is not helpful. Should\nget a new S/M – a lawyer + States will\npay for it.\n\nJustice O&#x27;Connor\nMaster should complete resolution of\nbasic data. Can quantify water\nby reliance on basic datas.</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1969 term</p><h2>Parker v. North Carolina</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/15f15d77-873b-4f09-a859-7a8946442ee5.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/1954\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Stewart, J. [struck: There was a] don&#x27;t\n[struck: so] think Jackson should\nbe given any impact at\nall on a plea of guilty.</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1969 term</p><h2>Standard Industries, Inc. v. Tigrett Industries, Inc., et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/95f5c6ee-ad67-4509-a2bf-d4361e6a5c23.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2007\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre><span class=\"wait\">No writing on this page.</span></pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1969 term</p><h2>United States v. Reynolds et Ux.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/46845a10-ecb2-49e8-af86-d3c6989abf7f.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2047\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>White, J.\nShotwell this\n&amp; save 20000\naward?</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1969 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by Lewis F. Powell Jr</p><h2>Breen v. Selective Service Local Board No. 16 et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/34b8609b-e751-4219-b3b3-2fac4f159a8e.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2117\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Texas v. New Mexico\nConf. 4/1/83\n\nThe Chief Justice\nCan&#x27;t agree with app&#x27;ting &quot;tie breaker&quot;.\n[struck: [illegible]] No [inserted: need to] write an opinion.\nDeny N.M. motion to dismiss\nHave Master reconsider the &quot;double\nmass analysis&quot;.\n\nJustice Brennan\n[struck: [illegible]] &quot;No&quot; as to tie-breaker.\nSpecial Master should redefine the\n&#x27;47 Condition + go ahead + decide issues\nNeed a new S/M.\n\nJustice White\nBreitstein is outraged by failure of\nlawyers to get together. [struck: R] He is very able.\n[struck: Pres is not]\nOn merits, we can&#x27;t app&#x27;t a tie breaker.\nNor do [underlined: we] have auth. to decide\nissues left to Comm.\nSustain whatever Exceptions are\n[struck: nec] necessary to return case to S/M.\nMust rely on Experts — this is\nan arbitrary choice</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1969 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by Lewis F. Powell Jr</p><h2>Breen v. Selective Service Local Board No. 16 et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/2e930fa6-07c3-4429-8728-6049f27d67af.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2117\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Justice Marshall\nAgree with B R W\n\nJustice Blackmun\nAgree generally with [struck: B] B R W\n\nJustice Powell\nSee my notes on p 2 of Report.</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1969 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by Lewis F. Powell Jr</p><h2>Breen v. Selective Service Local Board No. 16 et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/32eb5739-55fe-406a-baf0-b01a5c37ff20.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2117\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Justice Rehnquist\n[struck: Stat]\nNo Tiebreaker\nAgree with S/M as to double mass\n\nJustice Stevens\nS/M Report is not helpful. Should\nget a new S/M – a lawyer &amp; States will\npay for it.\n\nJustice O&#x27;Connor\nMaster should complete resolution of\nbasic data. Can quantify water\nby reliance on basic datas.</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term</p><h2>Perkins et al. v. Matthews, Mayor of the City of Canton, et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/d5c4db07-0266-4899-94a8-5c491218dbc9.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:3456/5184\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice Allen is directly in\npoint. changing lines &amp; polling\nplaces seems bad. But changing\nfrom ward to at large seems\ndifferent\n\nHarlan, J. Change of boundary\n[struck: not] precisely covered by\nAllen &amp; would affirm\nBut as to wards &amp;\nchanges of polling places\nthink they are little or\ndeminis.</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term</p><h2>Perkins et al. v. Matthews, Mayor of the City of Canton, et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/b1ba8ec9-6c63-4987-99fb-9e35356893a2.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:3456/5184\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Stewart, J. all three are tests &amp;\ndevices DC had no\npower under statute to\ndetermine whether\nthese devices had\npurpose &amp; effect of\ndiscrim. Second to\nAG or 3 judge court\nfor that. Would not\nenter conditional\ninjunction\n\nWhite, J.\nmore doubt about\nchange in polling\nplace than other\ntwo. On remedy,\nwouldn&#x27;t order another\nelection requiring\nelection which violates\nstate law. Courts remedy\nnot good one in Allen,\n&amp; if AG or 3 judge court\nfound polling places\nnon-discrim would\nlet election stand\n\nMarshall, J.\nWould</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term</p><h2>California v. Byers</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/57658eb0-b7d2-4214-8dae-375f81cd4719.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:3456/5184\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice Cal Sup Ct just plain\nwrong. In 20th Cent we come to a\ndead end if we can&#x27;t get driver\nto stop &amp; give his name &amp; use it\nto prosecute him. Whether\ndoing so is a condition to driver&#x27;s\nlicense, is just not testimonial\nwithin the Fifth Amend-\nment, state can exact it.\n\nBlack, J. To compel man by law\nto give evidence against\nhimself – would go beyond\n&amp; say statute wholly\nvoid under Fifth Amend\n\nDouglas, J. Never thought of law like\nthis in the criminal context\n– just that its part of whole\nregulation not gathered\nto make a criminal case\n\nHarlan, J. This is an extension\nof Marchetti &amp; Grosso. The\nStates broad interests entitle\nthem to have laws that\nrequire a driver to\nincriminate himself. I&#x27;d\nface up to it &amp; say so.\nThis is not a selective class\nof gamblers – the analogy\ncan be made to fit it but\nI won&#x27;t go that far</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term</p><h2>Amalgamated Association of Street, Electric Railway &amp; Motor Coach Employees of America et al. v. Lockridge</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/bcd7fd0c-3322-438c-bdb0-0ce8e8810f5e.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:3456/5184\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice Some problem as Ill.\nWrongful termination of union membership\ntheory relied on by State court to\ntake it outside preemption. Think\nthere ought be room for some\ndoctrine of equity — here equit-\ndoctrine against forfeiture\nhas a role. He can&#x27;t be\nthrown out without something\nlike equity of redemption. Here\nhe was only 24-48 hours delin-\nquent\n\nBlack, J. Don&#x27;t think there should\nbe a forfeiture on 24-48 hours\ndelinquency. But who is to hear\nthe claim? He could have attached\nhis [struck: expulsion], but instead sued\nfor damages. So under\nBorden &amp; Perko he had to go to\nNLRB\n\nDouglas, J. If he wanted reinstatement\nought go to NLRB. But if content\nto take damages, can sue\n\nHarlan, J.\nWould use this case to\noverrule Gonzales &amp; take\nGarmon as written in its\nfull sweep</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term</p><h2>Amalgamated Association of Street, Electric Railway &amp; Motor Coach Employees of America et al. v. Lockridge</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/98c2d2b3-56d5-4d21-9ad2-c5c8dd0cb98e.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:3456/5184\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>White, J.\nThink Garmon doctrine is\njust overbroad (1) in\narea where employer can&#x27;t\nget an NLRB remedy\n(2) and where, as in case\nof this chap&#x27;s colleague, the\nGeneral Counsel turns you\ndown when have a\ngood contract claim</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term</p><h2>United States v. Weller</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/0421002b-9333-433e-81fe-8a505b4f6038.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:3456/5184\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\nWe have juris, Regulation has\nsupport in the statute. Congress\nrefused to authorize counsel\nwhen statute was proposed.\nIf Goldberg v Kelly controls\nthen I&#x27;d follow it. But\nwould certify to Court of\nappeals</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term</p><h2>Palmer et al. v. Thompson, Mayor of the City of Jackson, et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/c9c60942-2b5c-4c5b-abff-50228e9b9775.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2250\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre><span class=\"wait\">No writing on this page.</span></pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1970 term</p><h2>Decker, U.s. District Judge, et al. v. Harper &amp; Row Publishers, Inc., et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/c3276ae7-dce9-4430-9e93-39fbf5ec4da9.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/2250\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre><span class=\"wait\">No writing on this page.</span></pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div c